From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Caleb E." <158400752+FoxesRCool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: surface_temp: Hide sensors that read 0 K

On the Surface Laptop 7 SAM lists temperature sensor instance 4 as
available (TMP available-sensors mask 0x0f1f) and answers its name
request ("I_RTS4"), but its temperature request always returns 0, i.e.
0 K. hwmon then shows it as -273.1 C. Instances SAM does not list time
out instead, so the mask itself is right: the sensor is listed but
not connected.

A reading of 0 K is not a real temperature. Return -ENODATA for it,
and leave a sensor out of the hwmon device when it reads 0 K at probe,
so sensors(1) and thermal tools no longer see a bogus channel. The
other channels keep their numbers.
---
 drivers/hwmon/surface_temp.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hwmon/surface_temp.c b/drivers/hwmon/surface_temp.c
index cd21f33..f5e1cf3 100644
--- a/drivers/hwmon/surface_temp.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/surface_temp.c
@@ -74,6 +74,14 @@ static int ssam_tmp_get_temperature(struct ssam_device *sdev, u8 iid, long *temp
 	if (status)
 		return status;
 
+	/*
+	 * Some sensors are listed as available but always read 0 (absolute
+	 * zero), e.g. instance 4 on the Surface Laptop 7. Report no data
+	 * instead of -273.1 °C.
+	 */
+	if (!le16_to_cpu(temp_le))
+		return -ENODATA;
+
 	/* Convert 1/10 °K to 1/1000 °C */
 	*temperature = (le16_to_cpu(temp_le) - 2731) * 100L;
 	return 0;
@@ -196,19 +204,29 @@ static int ssam_temp_probe(struct ssam_device *sdev)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
 	ssam_temp->sdev = sdev;
-	ssam_temp->sensors = sensors;
 
 	/* Retrieve the name for each available sensor. */
 	for (channel = 0; channel < SSAM_TMP_SENSOR_MAX_COUNT; channel++) {
+		long value;
+
 		if (!(sensors & BIT(channel)))
 			continue;
 
+		/* Hide sensors that are listed but not connected (read 0 K). */
+		if (ssam_tmp_get_temperature(sdev, channel + 1, &value) == -ENODATA) {
+			dev_dbg(&sdev->dev, "sensor %d reads 0 K, hiding it\n", channel + 1);
+			sensors &= ~BIT(channel);
+			continue;
+		}
+
 		status = ssam_tmp_get_name(sdev, channel + 1, ssam_temp->names[channel],
 					   SSAM_TMP_SENSOR_NAME_LENGTH);
 		if (status)
 			return status;
 	}
 
+	ssam_temp->sensors = sensors;
+
 	hwmon_dev = devm_hwmon_device_register_with_info(&sdev->dev, "surface_thermal", ssam_temp,
 							 &ssam_temp_hwmon_chip_info, NULL);
 	return PTR_ERR_OR_ZERO(hwmon_dev);
